.TH "HED-VIEWMD" "1" "2026-08-22" "hed v1.21.2" "hed manual"
.SH NAME
hed\-viewmd \- :viewmd opens a live HTML preview of the current Markdown
buffer in your default browser.
The preview reloads automatically as you save.
.PP
\f[CR]:viewmd\f[R] opens a live HTML preview of the current Markdown
buffer in your default browser.
The preview reloads automatically as you save.
.SH Usage
.IP
.EX
:viewmd          # open the current buffer\[aq]s preview
.EE
.PP
Default leader binding: \f[CR]<space>rp\f[R].
.SH How it works
The plugin starts a small local HTTP server bound to a random loopback
port, generates an HTML page from the buffer\[cq]s contents on each
request, and points your browser at the URL.
A \f[CR]HOOK_BUFFER_SAVE\f[R] handler triggers a soft reload via a
long\-polling endpoint.
.PP
The server is per\-buffer \[em] switching to another buffer and running
\f[CR]:viewmd\f[R] starts a second server.
When the buffer is closed, its server is torn down.
.SH Requirements
.IP \[bu] 2
A working browser\-launch path (\f[CR]xdg\-open\f[R], \f[CR]open\f[R],
or \f[CR]start\f[R] depending on platform).
.IP \[bu] 2
An available loopback port.
The plugin asks the kernel for one; no configuration needed.
.SH Notes
.IP \[bu] 2
The preview is read\-only \[em] there\[cq]s no edit\-in\-browser.
Edit in hed; saved changes flow to the preview.
.IP \[bu] 2
If your buffer\[cq]s filetype isn\[cq]t \f[CR]markdown\f[R], the preview
still works but the conversion is a best\-effort plain\-text wrap.
.IP \[bu] 2
Stop a preview by closing its browser tab \[em] the server stays
running, but its only purpose is to serve that tab.
(Closing the buffer kills the server cleanly.)
